On x32 glibc computes the page counts for sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES) and
sysconf(_SC_AVPHYS_PAGES) with a 32-bit long, so on a machine with more than
4 GiB of RAM both wrap around and the reported total comes out smaller than
the reported available memory, which is what this test checks.  Not a bug in
coreutils; drop this once glibc handles x32 correctly.

--- coreutils-9.12/gnulib-tests/gnulib.mk.orig
+++ coreutils-9.12/gnulib-tests/gnulib.mk
@@ -2668,7 +2668,6 @@
 
 ## begin gnulib module physmem-tests
 
-TESTS += test-physmem
 check_PROGRAMS += test-physmem
 EXTRA_DIST += test-physmem.c macros.h
 
